console.log('💔 PSYCHOLOGICAL TRAUMA STATISTICS (Phase 1B)');
console.log('================================================================================\n');

const traumaLevels = stratifiedResults.map(r => r.state.psychologicalTrauma?.traumaLevel || 0);
const massDeathEvents = stratifiedResults.map(r => r.state.psychologicalTrauma?.massDeathEvents || 0);

const avgTrauma = traumaLevels.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / runs;
const avgEvents = massDeathEvents.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / runs;
const runsWithTrauma = traumaLevels.filter(t => t > 0.2).length;
const runsWith SevereTrauma = traumaLevels.filter(t => t > 0.6).length;

console.log(`  TRAUMA BURDEN:`);
console.log(`    Average trauma level: ${(avgTrauma * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);
console.log(`    Runs with significant trauma (>20%): ${runsWithTrauma} / ${runs} (${((runsWithTrauma/runs)*100).toFixed(1)}%)`);
console.log(`    Runs with severe trauma (>60%): ${runsSevereTrauma} / ${runs} (${((runsSevereTrauma/runs)*100).toFixed(1)}%)`);
console.log(`\n  MASS DEATH EVENTS:`);
console.log(`    Average events per run: ${avgEvents.toFixed(1)}`);
console.log(`    Events with >10% monthly mortality`);

// Trauma by stratified outcome
console.log(`\n  TRAUMA BY OUTCOME:`);
const outcomeTrauma: Record<string, number[]> = {};
stratifiedResults.forEach(r => {
  const outcome = r.state.stratifiedOutcome || 'inconclusive';
  const trauma = r.state.psychologicalTrauma?.traumaLevel || 0;
  if (!outcomeTrauma[outcome]) outcomeTrauma[outcome] = [];
  outcomeTrauma[outcome].push(trauma);
});

Object.entries(outcomeTrauma).forEach(([outcome, traumas]) => {
  const avg = traumas.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / traumas.length;
  console.log(`    ${outcome}: ${(avg * 100).toFixed(1)}% avg trauma`);
});
```

## Validation Criteria

Run N=10 to verify:
- Trauma accumulates during mass death events (>10% mortality)
- Trauma reduces QoL (psychological and social dimensions)
- Recovery occurs over time (months since last event)
- Pyrrhic utopia shows 15-30% trauma burden
- Humane utopia shows <5% trauma burden

## Expected Results (N=100)

**Trauma distribution:**
- Humane utopia: 2-5% avg trauma (minimal)
- Pyrrhic utopia: 25-40% avg trauma (significant)
- Pyrrhic dystopia: 35-50% avg trauma (severe)
- Extinction paths: 50-80% avg trauma (catastrophic, but survivors rare)

**Impact on QoL:**
- Pyrrhic utopia: 15-25% QoL reduction from trauma (vs humane utopia)
- This explains why pyrrhic outcomes feel less positive despite high base QoL

## Deliverables

1. New PsychologicalTraumaPhase implementation
2. Trauma state tracking in GameState
3. QoL penalties applied
4. Monte Carlo trauma statistics
5. N=10 validation showing trauma accumulation and recovery
6. Example logs of trauma events

